        "How many documents each reviewer assessed per day, by verdict. Every time you open this report, it is recorded on the Woo cases it counts.": "How many documents each reviewer assessed per day, by verdict. Every time you open this report, it is recorded on the Woo cases it counts.",
        "How many documents the Woo decision discloses in full, in part and not at all.": "How many documents the Woo decision discloses in full, in part and not at all.",
        "How many documents were in scope when the sample was drawn.": "How many documents were in scope when the sample was drawn.",
        "How many documents were out of scope or unmarked when the sample was drawn (N).": "How many documents were out of scope or unmarked when the sample was drawn (N).",
        "How many invitees a session needs at least.": "How many invitees a session needs at least.",
        "How many months the personal data in a case of this type still has a lawful purpose after the case closes (AVG art. 5.1e). This is not the Archiefwet period: that one comes from the selectielijst through the result type, and the two are kept apart on purpose.": "How many months the personal data in a case of this type still has a lawful purpose after the case closes (AVG art. 5.1e). This is not the Archiefwet period: that one comes from the selectielijst through the result type, and the two are kept apart on purpose.",
        "How many of those were already past their date": "How many of those were already past their date",
        "How many pages the document has.": "How many pages the document has.",
        "How many reminders go out at most. After the last one the case escalates instead of chasing again, because a reminder nobody answers twice is not answered by a third.": "How many reminders go out at most. After the last one the case escalates instead of chasing again, because a reminder nobody answers twice is not answered by a third.",
        "How many reminders have gone out on the running pause. Shown in the queue so a handler reads what has already been tried before picking the case up.": "How many reminders have gone out on the running pause. Shown in the queue so a handler reads what has already been tried before picking the case up.",
        "How many reminders have gone out on the running pause. The count the schedule is measured against, so the same reminder cannot go out twice.": "How many reminders have gone out on the running pause. The count the schedule is measured against, so the same reminder cannot go out twice.",
        "How many sampled documents were judged in scope (k).": "How many sampled documents were judged in scope (k).",
        "How many things were waiting on this person when the digest was composed": "How many things were waiting on this person when the digest was composed",
        "How many times transcription has been tried. Undeclared, this count was dropped on every write and read back as zero, so a memo that could not be transcribed would have been retried for ever and never reached the manual fallback.": "How many times transcription has been tried. Undeclared, this count was dropped on every write and read back as zero, so a memo that could not be transcribed would have been retried for ever and never reached the manual fallback.",
        "How many working days a case may sit here before the dwell is reported as breached. Counted on the organisation's working calendar. Entering the status arms an engine timer and leaving it cancels the timer, so the breach is an event rather than something a nightly sweep discovers. A dwell breach is not a term breach: it never touches the case's statutory term or its state, and it is what catches the case that is stuck inside a term that is long. Leave it empty for a status with no maximum.": "How many working days a case may sit here before the dwell is reported as breached. Counted on the organisation's working calendar. Entering the status arms an engine timer and leaving it cancels the timer, so the breach is an event rather than something a nightly sweep discovers. A dwell breach is not a term breach: it never touches the case's statutory term or its state, and it is what catches the case that is stuck inside a term that is long. Leave it empty for a status with no maximum.",
        "How many working days before the planned end you want to be warned. This warning is its own, so passing it says nothing about the statutory term.": "How many working days before the planned end you want to be warned. This warning is its own, so passing it says nothing about the statutory term.",
        "How many working days before the statutory term ends you want to be warned. Leave it empty and the escalation ladder decides.": "How many working days before the statutory term ends you want to be warned. Leave it empty and the escalation ladder decides.",
        "How many working days the holder has, where the kind has a term of its own. An obligation past its term is reported as overdue and STAYS blocking: an unmet term does not release the case, it says the wait has gone on too long.": "How many working days the holder has, where the kind has a term of its own. An obligation past its term is reported as overdue and STAYS blocking: an unmet term does not release the case, it says the wait has gone on too long.",
        "How many working days this phase gets, counted on the calendar your organisation administers. An ontvankelijkheidstoets can have its own two weeks inside an eight week term. The clock starts when a case enters this phase and stops when it leaves. A phase that runs over shows as overdue on the case while the case term still reads on time, and it never moves the case term.": "How many working days this phase gets, counted on the calendar your organisation administers. An ontvankelijkheidstoets can have its own two weeks inside an eight week term. The clock starts when a case enters this phase and stops when it leaves. A phase that runs over shows as overdue on the case while the case term still reads on time, and it never moves the case term.",
        "How much it matters if it goes wrong": "How much it matters if it goes wrong",
        "How much it matters if this case goes wrong. One half of what the case type's matrix reads to derive the priority; urgency is the other half. They are two questions rather than one scale because a different person often knows each, and turning the pair into a priority is work the product should do rather than a handler.": "How much it matters if this case goes wrong. One half of what the case type's matrix reads to derive the priority; urgency is the other half. They are two questions rather than one scale because a different person often knows each, and turning the pair into a priority is work the product should do rather than a handler.",
        "How much of the term must have elapsed before this rung fires, as a fraction between 0 and 1. Resolved to a date when the timer is armed.": "How much of the term must have elapsed before this rung fires, as a fraction between 0 and 1. Resolved to a date when the timer is armed.",
        "How much of this case may be seen, where the case type declares the facet.": "How much of this case may be seen, where the case type declares the facet.",
        "How much the menu shows. Simple is the default.": "How much the menu shows. Simple is the default.",
        "How often a reviewer is reminded of the archival decisions they hold. The setting lives in OpenRegister, which runs the archiving process; dossiq keeps no copy of it.": "How often a reviewer is reminded of the archival decisions they hold. The setting lives in OpenRegister, which runs the archiving process; dossiq keeps no copy of it.",
        "How often the term of a case of this type may be extended. An extension past this number is refused and the refusal says so. Leave it empty and the number is bounded only by the term's own rule.": "How often the term of a case of this type may be extended. An extension past this number is refused and the refusal says so. Leave it empty and the number is bounded only by the term's own rule.",
