        "How the team is doing · {dateRange}, all teams you are in": "How the team is doing · {dateRange}, all teams you are in",
        "How this case is shared: a public access link, a partner organisation handover, or the retired token. ADR-037 concatenates enum values, so `token` and `partner` keep their places.": "How this case is shared: a public access link, a partner organisation handover, or the retired token. ADR-037 concatenates enum values, so `token` and `partner` keep their places.",
        "How this case was last routed to a person: the rule (strategy, roleType or roleTypes, team, areaTeams, fallback, and the optional take-back window `takeBackAfter` {value, unit: hours|businessDays|calendarDays}), who it went to and when, and when that person accepted it. Accepting is the assignee's first status move or first edit of the case; there is no accept button (decision 164). While `acceptedAt` is empty and the rule declares a window, an engine timer is armed: when it passes, the case returns to the pool and is routed on by the same rule.": "How this case was last routed to a person: the rule (strategy, roleType or roleTypes, team, areaTeams, fallback, and the optional take-back window `takeBackAfter` {value, unit: hours|businessDays|calendarDays}), who it went to and when, and when that person accepted it. Accepting is the assignee's first status move or first edit of the case; there is no accept button (decision 164). While `acceptedAt` is empty and the rule declares a window, an engine timer is armed: when it passes, the case returns to the pool and is routed on by the same rule.",
        "How this endpoint authenticates. WSSE UsernameToken is the StUF default.": "How this endpoint authenticates. WSSE UsernameToken is the StUF default.",
        "How this party is reached. Each address carries a kind: correspondence is what outbound mail picks, case is the address the case is about, location is a point on the map. Inbound mail from any of them resolves to this party, so a second record is never created.": "How this party is reached. Each address carries a kind: correspondence is what outbound mail picks, case is the address the case is about, location is a point on the map. Inbound mail from any of them resolves to this party, so a second record is never created.",
