        "The group of case types this one belongs to. A samenwerkingsverband grants once on the group and every type in it inherits the grant, so thirty grants that drift become one. The inheritance is OpenRegister's (rbac-inherits-to-children): dossiq declares the membership and never re-applies a group grant to each type.": "The group of case types this one belongs to. A samenwerkingsverband grants once on the group and every type in it inherits the grant, so thirty grants that drift become one. The inheritance is OpenRegister's (rbac-inherits-to-children): dossiq declares the membership and never re-applies a group grant to each type.",
        "The group of similar reports this case was placed in by hermiq, when its case type groups reports. Grouping does not change the confirmations of receipt: every report still gets its own.": "The group of similar reports this case was placed in by hermiq, when its case type groups reports. Grouping does not change the confirmations of receipt: every report still gets its own.",
        "The group that handles it from here": "The group that handles it from here",
        "The group that owns the private records, reads all of them and may change any of them.": "The group that owns the private records, reads all of them and may change any of them.",
        "The group whose members may abort a case of this type. An abort records an intrekking or a niet-ontvankelijkverklaring: there is a result and it is not a besluit. Named separately from finishing because the two are not the same authority.": "The group whose members may abort a case of this type. An abort records an intrekking or a niet-ontvankelijkverklaring: there is a result and it is not a besluit. Named separately from finishing because the two are not the same authority.",
        "The group whose members may archive a finished case of this type. Archiving writes the retention rule the result type carries, so it is an archivist's act rather than a handler's. A case type that names no group refuses every archive except an administrator's.": "The group whose members may archive a finished case of this type. Archiving writes the retention rule the result type carries, so it is an archivist's act rather than a handler's. A case type that names no group refuses every archive except an administrator's.",
        "The group whose members may destroy a deleted case of this type. Destroying is a second act after deleting, and it cannot be undone, so the right is named per case type: a melding and a bezwaar do not need the same seniority behind it. A case type that names no group refuses every destruction except an administrator's, which is the same answer OpenRegister's own destroy right gives.": "The group whose members may destroy a deleted case of this type. Destroying is a second act after deleting, and it cannot be undone, so the right is named per case type: a melding and a bezwaar do not need the same seniority behind it. A case type that names no group refuses every destruction except an administrator's, which is the same answer OpenRegister's own destroy right gives.",
        "The group whose members may finish a case of this type. Finishing is the act that says the case reached its result, and the result decides what is retained. A case type that names no group lets any handler with access to the case finish it, which is today's behaviour.": "The group whose members may finish a case of this type. Finishing is the act that says the case reached its result, and the result decides what is retained. A case type that names no group lets any handler with access to the case finish it, which is today's behaviour.",
        "The groups and the people that may be chosen as the handler when a case of this type is created. Declaring neither keeps every choice.": "The groups and the people that may be chosen as the handler when a case of this type is created. Declaring neither keeps every choice.",
        "The groups that keep the field. This is the opposite list to the one above, and it is deliberately not derived from it: naming who loses a field says nothing about who keeps it unless you know every group on the server, which a case type does not. A group written in both lists loses the field. That resolution is visible to the person it affects, and the other one hands the field to somebody the author wrote down as restricted.": "The groups that keep the field. This is the opposite list to the one above, and it is deliberately not derived from it: naming who loses a field says nothing about who keeps it unless you know every group on the server, which a case type does not. A group written in both lists loses the field. That resolution is visible to the person it affects, and the other one hands the field to somebody the author wrote down as restricted.",
        "The groups the rule takes the field away from. Leave it empty and no rule is published for them, because a rule naming nobody applies to everybody, administrators included. This list is the one the case lifecycle reads, and it is a list of who LOSES the field.": "The groups the rule takes the field away from. Leave it empty and no rule is published for them, because a rule naming nobody applies to everybody, administrators included. This list is the one the case lifecycle reads, and it is a list of who LOSES the field.",
        "The handler who asked. Written from the session rather than offered as a field, so nobody signs somebody else's name to a statutory act.": "The handler who asked. Written from the session rather than offered as a field, so nobody signs somebody else's name to a statutory act.",
