        "What one entry of a list looks like, as {\"type\": \"string\"}. Only used when the type is array. The vocabulary's 'items' key takes a shape rather than a type name, so storing the name alone would forward something malformed.": "What one entry of a list looks like, as {\"type\": \"string\"}. Only used when the type is array. The vocabulary's 'items' key takes a shape rather than a type name, so storing the name alone would forward something malformed.",
        "What outcome does the objector seek?": "What outcome does the objector seek?",
        "What outcome the bezwaarmaker seeks": "What outcome the bezwaarmaker seeks",
