        "Who is to do it, resolved from the type's role on the case at the moment it was planned.": "Who is to do it, resolved from the type's role on the case at the moment it was planned.",
        "Who it affects": "Who it affects",
        "Who it is lodged with, as the clause names them, for example het college van burgemeester en wethouders.": "Who it is lodged with, as the clause names them, for example het college van burgemeester en wethouders.",
        "Who made the assessment.": "Who made the assessment.",
        "Who made the move that opened this holding.": "Who made the move that opened this holding.",
        "Who made this move. Written by the engine on every transition, and read by the four-eyes rule: a transition may declare an earlier act whose performer may not make it, and the performer is read from this chain rather than inferred. A record written before this property existed falls back to the object owner, so the rule binds history that already exists rather than only cases started afterwards.": "Who made this move. Written by the engine on every transition, and read by the four-eyes rule: a transition may declare an earlier act whose performer may not make it, and the performer is read from this chain rather than inferred. A record written before this property existed falls back to the object owner, so the rule binds history that already exists rather than only cases started afterwards.",
        "Who may change it, for example client for a resident.": "Who may change it, for example client for a resident.",
        "Who may do what with cases of this type": "Who may do what with cases of this type",
        "Who may do what with cases of this type, as a matrix of department by role, separately per confidentiality level. Confidentiality is an AXIS of this declaration and is never folded into a role name: a role per level per department is the combinatorial explosion every mandate matrix eventually becomes. Declared here and evaluated in OpenRegister, which owns the grant, its provenance and the deny. dossiq computes no effective permission from these rows.": "Who may do what with cases of this type, as a matrix of department by role, separately per confidentiality level. Confidentiality is an AXIS of this declaration and is never folded into a role name: a role per level per department is the combinatorial explosion every mandate matrix eventually becomes. Declared here and evaluated in OpenRegister, which owns the grant, its provenance and the deny. dossiq computes no effective permission from these rows.",
        "Who may handle this": "Who may handle this",
        "Who on the case reads the record. All: the assignee and every reviewer. Assignee: the assignee only. Own: the assignee and the reviewers the record names. Supervisors always read it.": "Who on the case reads the record. All: the assignee and every reviewer. Assignee: the assignee only. Own: the assignee and the reviewers the record names. Supervisors always read it.",
        "Who pays a forfeited penalty": "Who pays a forfeited penalty",
