        "Who sent this document, as a party of this case in the role afzender. Holds the party's uuid, or the contact uid of a link written before the party model. An incoming document gets one from the mail intake; you can set or correct it in the document's properties.": "Who sent this document, as a party of this case in the role afzender. Holds the party's uuid, or the contact uid of a link written before the party model. An incoming document gets one from the mail intake; you can set or correct it in the document's properties.",
        "Who set the override. Written from the session rather than offered as a field, because who made a decision is a fact about the edit and not something anybody should be able to type.": "Who set the override. Written from the session rather than offered as a field, because who made a decision is a fact about the edit and not something anybody should be able to type.",
        "Who set the relevance.": "Who set the relevance.",
        "Who takes over the cases of an absent handler, and the bulk reassignment of their work.": "Who takes over the cases of an absent handler, and the bulk reassignment of their work.",
        "Who the case belongs to in the portal: a person (subject:) or a company (kvk:).": "Who the case belongs to in the portal: a person (subject:) or a company (kvk:).",
        "Who the case waits on while it sits here. The applicant and a third party are DIFFERENT facts: a hersteltermijn suspends the beslistermijn and an advice request does not, so a value that conflates them cannot decide whether the clock stops. Queue and team counts read this. The role property keeps working unchanged beside it; leave waitingOn empty and the case counts as ours to move.": "Who the case waits on while it sits here. The applicant and a third party are DIFFERENT facts: a hersteltermijn suspends the beslistermijn and an advice request does not, so a value that conflates them cannot decide whether the clock stops. Queue and team counts read this. The role property keeps working unchanged beside it; leave waitingOn empty and the case counts as ours to move.",
        "Who the case waits on while it sits here. The applicant and a third party are different: only the first suspends the term.": "Who the case waits on while it sits here. The applicant and a third party are different: only the first suspends the term.",
        "Who the message is for. On a handler's message (handler_to_citizen) it is the case's portalSubject, never a user id: the resident's portal inbox is scoped on it. On a resident's message it names the handler, when known.": "Who the message is for. On a handler's message (handler_to_citizen) it is the case's portalSubject, never a user id: the resident's portal inbox is scoped on it. On a resident's message it names the handler, when known.",
        "Who the resident is told is at turn: applicant while we wait on them, thirdParty while we wait on somebody else, us otherwise, and empty once the case is closed.": "Who the resident is told is at turn: applicant while we wait on them, thirdParty while we wait on somebody else, us otherwise, and empty once the case is closed.",
        "Who the resident is told is at turn: applicant while we wait on them, thirdParty while we wait on somebody else, us otherwise, and empty once the case is closed. It is calculated from the end date and what the status waits on. The words the resident reads are set per portal, not here.": "Who the resident is told is at turn: applicant while we wait on them, thirdParty while we wait on somebody else, us otherwise, and empty once the case is closed. It is calculated from the end date and what the status waits on. The words the resident reads are set per portal, not here.",
        "Who the resident says they are asking as: burger, journalist or organisatie. It is what they chose, not a judgement we make.": "Who the resident says they are asking as: burger, journalist or organisatie. It is what they chose, not a judgement we make.",
        "Who the running pause waits on, taken from the reason in force. Held here as well as on the reason because a reason can be re-declared and a pause that already ran has to keep reading the way it was registered.": "Who the running pause waits on, taken from the reason in force. Held here as well as on the reason because a reason can be re-declared and a pause that already ran has to keep reading the way it was registered.",
        "Who this case is waiting on right now, from the reason of the running pause. A read convenience over the term instances, never a second truth: the queue has to narrow on it without reading every instance of every case.": "Who this case is waiting on right now, from the reason of the running pause. A read convenience over the term instances, never a second truth: the queue has to narrow on it without reading every instance of every case.",
        "Who this case waits on, taken from the status it sits in (statusType.waitingOn).": "Who this case waits on, taken from the status it sits in (statusType.waitingOn).",
        "Who this case waits on, taken from the status it sits in (statusType.waitingOn). Computed declaratively by OpenRegister so a queue counts by it server-side rather than by reading four hundred rows into PHP. A status that declares nothing reads as ours to move, which is what makes the count safe on a case type nobody has annotated. After editing a statusType's waitingOn, run occ openregister:rematerialise-calculations.": "Who this case waits on, taken from the status it sits in (statusType.waitingOn). Computed declaratively by OpenRegister so a queue counts by it server-side rather than by reading four hundred rows into PHP. A status that declares nothing reads as ours to move, which is what makes the count safe on a case type nobody has annotated. After editing a statusType's waitingOn, run occ openregister:rematerialise-calculations.",
        "Who this document went to, as parties of this case in the role geadresseerde. Each entry holds the party's uuid, or the contact uid of a link written before the party model. An outgoing document gets them from the send that filed it; you can set or correct them in the document's properties.": "Who this document went to, as parties of this case in the role geadresseerde. Each entry holds the party's uuid, or the contact uid of a link written before the party model. An outgoing document gets them from the send that filed it; you can set or correct them in the document's properties.",
        "Who this message came from, as a party of the case in the role afzender. Empty when no party of the case holds the From address: the intake does not create a party for every stranger who mails the case.": "Who this message came from, as a party of the case in the role afzender. Empty when no party of the case holds the From address: the intake does not create a party for every stranger who mails the case.",
        "Who took the approving transition. Written by the engine's status record chain and copied here so the run can refuse without walking that chain. Never the person who prepared the preview: the transition declares `notPerformedBy` against the preparing act.": "Who took the approving transition. Written by the engine's status record chain and copied here so the run can refuse without walking that chain. Never the person who prepared the preview: the transition declares `notPerformedBy` against the preparing act.",
